course: dictionary
lesson: 9065
title: Slim: kind, small, or slimming down
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word slim has several meanings, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. Its most common job is to describe something thin in a neat or healthy way: «The fossa is Madagascar's biggest meat-eater, shaped like a slim cat.» Slim sounds kinder than skinny.
explain: Slim can also mean small in amount. In «a slim chance» or «a slim lead», the clue is the word little: a team with a slim lead is only just ahead. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The team had a slim lead» means only a small amount ahead, so it works.
explain: As a verb, slim means to try to lose weight by eating less, or to make smaller. «The school slimmed down the timetable» means the school reduced it. Check by swapping in make smaller: it still makes sense.
fact: «Slim» means thin in an attractive or healthy way, or small in amount.
fact: «Slim» is a kinder word than «skinny» when you describe a person.
fact: «A slim chance» means only a small chance.
fact: «Slim down» means to make smaller or reduce.
fact: Health lessons teach that bodies come in all shapes and that being healthy matters more than being slim.
exercise: «Bonobos look like slim chimpanzees.» What does slim mean here? | *Thin in a neat, attractive way | Very large and heavy | Loud and noisy | Wet and muddy
exercise: Ella says a team with a «slim lead» is far ahead. Is she right? | No, slim means lost | Yes, it means the game has finished | *No, a slim lead means only a little ahead | Yes, slim means very far ahead
exercise: Which phrase means to make smaller or reduce? | *slim down | slim volume | slim chance | slim cat
test: Why might a writer choose «slim» instead of «skinny»? | Because slim is longer | *Because slim is a kinder word for thin | Because slim means very old | Because skinny means fast
test: «Young ones were slimmer and faster.» What does slimmer mean here? | *Thinner, with less weight | Louder | Older and slower | Bigger and heavier
exam: Mia says «a slim chance» means a big chance. What does it really mean? | A chance to win a prize | A chance to dance | A very big chance | *Only a small chance
